      "answer": "From the offline source:\nWe keep 12 liters of drinking water per person in the three blue barrels in the garage, next to the bicycles. That covers the four of us for about three days. The barrels are emptied and refilled twice a year, in March and in September, when the clocks change. To treat tap or rain water we use 2 drops of unscented household bleach per liter and wait 30 minutes before drinking. The ceramic filter lives in the kitchen cabinet above the sink. Meeting points If we get separated at home, we meet at the mango tree at the corner of Rua das Flores. If the neighborhood has to be evacuated, the meeting point is the parish hall of São José, two kilometers north. [1]\n\nIn an emergency, call your local emergency number (911 in the US, 112 in Europe)."
